# A ~60s lesson, written to be recorded and shared.
# The arc: real pain -> obvious fix -> the cost nobody mentions -> the trade.
#
# Note the ordering: the claim is spoken, then the ink that proves it goes down
# while the words are still in the air. A `say` stacked after its own shapes is
# a caption, and the board is frozen while it plays.
board 64 36

say "You added one index, and the app got slower. That is not a bug."
text 3,2.5 "You added an index. The app got slower. How?"

# --- the pain that makes you reach for an index
say "Finding one row means reading all five million. That is the pain."
icon db 10,13 7 "users"
text 20,10 "5,000,000 rows"
text 20,13 "WHERE email = ..."
arrow 19,16 30,16 "scan every row"
icon clock 36,16 6 "slow"
highlight "slow" "Everybody has felt this one."

# --- the obvious fix
say "An index is a second copy of that column, kept in sorted order."
text 3,24 "So you add an index:"
box 3,27 18,3 "CREATE INDEX ..."
icon file 32,27.5 5 "sorted copy"
connect "CREATE INDEX ..." "sorted copy" "builds"
say "Now the lookup is a handful of comparisons. Genuinely faster."

# --- the turn: what nobody puts in the tutorial
pan 36
say "But look at what every write now has to do."
text 3,39 "One insert. Two structures to keep true."
icon file 10,48 6 "INSERT"
icon db 28,48 7 "table"
icon file 48,48 6 "index"
connect "INSERT" "table" "write 1"
connect "table" "index" "write 2"
highlight "index" "This is the write you did not know you were buying."

say "And this is the part the tutorial leaves out."
text 3,58 "Five indexes on that table means six writes per insert."
box 3,62 26,3 "just add more indexes"
strike "just add more indexes" "So this is where it stops being free."
say "Reads got faster. Writes got slower. You did not break it -- you traded."
note 33,62 28 "An index is not a setting. It is a second structure you now own, and pay for on every write."
